-Well, there's a first!

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.700
I am going to give you a point for Mars [DING]
He was one of the people who...

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.080
Canals on Mars?

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.860
-Point! [DING] Absolutely right.
-There we go!

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.360
Percival Lowell in America, was the
 one who came up with the theory.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.380
But yes, he thought there were artificial canals on Mars.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:00.840
What? For boating?

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.800
Yeah! Big, big canal boating system.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.220
Big recreational holiday market out there, to be honest.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:09.220
Go to Mars. Get a narrowboat.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.260
Pootle along the canals of Mars.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.400
At a gentle four miles per Mars hour.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.320
The canals on Mars were actually what?

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.300
Motorways.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:20.140
Just rain covered motorways. When they looked at them through the telescope, the light glinted off them.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.560
-It was an easy mistake. Anyone could have made it.
-Swans landing on it, all the time.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:23.760
All the bloody time.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:24.960
Cobwebs on the telescope?

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.760
Erm... not quite.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.060
Not quite.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.020
They were natural formations, weren't they?

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:32.940
No!

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.860
No, not at all. 
And they weren't artificial formations either.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.980
So they weren't formations at all!

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.980
I will give you a point. [DING]

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.140
Can you explain what they were?

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:42.740
No!

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.580
I was just being a pedant about what you'd said.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.580
There are two possible explanations for the canals.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:49.380
-One...
-They're canals!

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.720
OK, there are three...

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:55.080
But one of them was definitely wrong.
 There are still two, that are... possibly...

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:59.320
One is that there was a formation... 
something they saw, they misinterpreted.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.180
The other...

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.540
is an optical illusion.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.960
Like the one when you go to the fair and you walk in and the mirror makes you look all small and fat?

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.780
Yeah, that it made a load of...

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:10.880
Watch it! Watch it, watch it... 
Watch it!

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:16.860
It made a load of points look like lines that
connected up, through a slightly dodgy telescope.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.520
But! Why canals?

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.820
It could have been rivers or...

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.260
-They were straight lines.
-They were very straight.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.780
So they looked more like canals than rivers.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.560
So they looked like irrigation canals.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:30.600
You know what? If I had the ability to do
one gigantic s***-stirring effort

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:34.240
I would now transport myself to Mars...
with a canal boat!

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.300
Just be there waving.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.920
No. Put it out on Mars and half bury it, 
like it's been there a long time.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.400
When the next Mars rover comes over the hill.
"Holy s***!"

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.100
I suppose the Curiosity rover's the size of a big car.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:48.760
Yeah!

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:51.760
So if you make it shorter and longer, 
it's a narrowboat rover.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.460
If you just put, I don't know, some...

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:57.380
expanding foam sealant around the windows and doors. I'm sure it would be airtight enough.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:01.500
I mean let's face it, the moon lander was
 made of tin foil. A canal boat's way stronger!

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.020
Hello NASA?

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.460
Yes, it's Matt Gray.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.380
Put narrowboats on Mars.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:07.840
They've gone.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.200
See, this is how the world gets sorted.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.160
Yeah! Matt Gray.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.940
"Hello World Organisation, it is Matt Gray!"

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:18.840
So... Flammarion was...

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:26.140
I'm going to try...
I'm going to try.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.080
I'm not even off tangent. 
We're talking about canals on Mars.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.340
Yeah, yeah!

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:32.620
Oh yeah!

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:34.540
This is perfectly on stream!

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.220
How did we stay relevant?!

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:37.980
It's a skill!

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.840
I dunno? Six years later, how are we still relevant?

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:48.100
Flammarion was both scientist and...
 very much not a scientist.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.380
So he was exposed to
two very different lines of thought.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:56.840
One of them was very much scientific method.
Who in his era would have been

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.120
the person, standing at the front of,
"this is science against religion"?

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.160
The chief scientist?

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.360
Darwin!

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:06.000
Point. [DING] Exactly right. 
And then on the other hand,

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:11.660
the rising popularity of what
less scientific movement?

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:12.580
Roller skating?

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.180
Not really... 
I mean, it is a movement!

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:19.240
Very movement! Straight line,
forwards or backwards. Yes.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:20.220
Bowel?

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.940
Not a bowel movement! No, we're not having...

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.360
Chris, save us!

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:26.140
Cubism?

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:29.540
Way too early.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:33.080
I don't know!

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.440
Spiritualism.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:38.380
-The idea that...
-"Knock three times...."

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.320
Yes, the idea that you could talk to the dead.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.380
So he was astronomer, mystic and story teller.
In a time when...

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:47.080
Liar, liar... and liar!

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:48.760
No, astronomer!

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:54.740
This is the thing. This is where astronomy and astrology
hadn't quite sorted each other out yet.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:55.760
Diverged, yeah.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:06:02.480
So in 1907, he wrote that dwellers on Mars
had tried to communicate with the Earth.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:03.420
Naturally.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:06.340
And also that what was heading towards Earth?

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.360
-Cylinders...
-Following cylinders!

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.500
No one would have believed in the last
 years of the nineteenth century

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.740
that canals on Mars were being observed...

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:22.460
No. Not in this case.
Something from a little bit further out.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:24.360
Asteroid?

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:24.860
Asteroid.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:25.880
Aste... Uranus?!

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:27.680
You're very close with asteroid.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:28.560
Comet?

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:30.540
Point! [DING] for that. Comet is absolutely right.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.760
A seven tailed comet.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:35.200
Are you sure that's not just a very
 badly focused telescope again?

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.460
Well that was the thing, yes!

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:40.540
It seems to be swirling in a spiral!

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:43.860
A small comet's seen, it did not have seven tails.

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.840
"He's using the kaleidoscope again, isn't he?"

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:49.800
They are in a formation, where there
 is one at the top, one on each side...

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.680
and there is an upside down one at the bottom.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.280
Oh ****ing hell! Giant spiders in space!

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.980
Along those lines, 1910, what
astronomical event revisited us?

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:00.760
Halley's.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:02.860
Yeah, you got there first again, have a point. [DING]

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.660
He caused a bit of a fuss, did Flammarion.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:09.440
Earth was actually going to pass through
 the tail of Halley's comet. For the first time.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:14.340
And we also, for the first time, had
spectroscopic data on what it was composed of.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.920
So they looked at the light coming
out of it, to find out what...

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:20.600
To find out what elements and what stuff
was in the tail, that Earth was going to pass through.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:21.740
I'm surprised they could do that then.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:22.860
Yep! 1910.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:25.480
It's the first time they were able to do it.
 So it was a close approach.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:28.220
We were passing through the tail.
What did Flammarion say...

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:29.740
"We're all going to die!"

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:30.700
Point! [DING]

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.160
But how?

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:35.380
Bearing in mind they now knew what the tail was composed of and what some of the stuff...

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:37.040
Poisoning! Asphyxiation!

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.540
Yes! Absolutely right. Poison gas.
 [DING]

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:46.520
There was a cyanogen, which is (CN)₂.
There are brackets there, so it's 2 of each.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.480
Colourless, toxic gas.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:51.380
And apparently he thought
"well that's in the tail of the comet."

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:53.380
"We're going to pass through the tail of the comet."

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:55.480
"WE'RE ALL GOING TO DIE!"

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:57.780
He was wrong.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:07:59.300
Hello!

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:00.640
No way! Really?

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:06.600
He said it would impregnate the atmosphere and possibly snuff out all life on the planet.

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:08.760
Did he use the words 'snuff out'?

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:09.360
Erm, I...

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:11.380
-I hope so.
-Being French...

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:12.760
"Ze snuff."

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:14.400
I would have thought he would have done that in French.

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:15.820
I believe that is a translation.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:17.980
"C'est buggered!"

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.040
What did it cause?

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:22.340
PANIC!

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:24.400
To a certain extent. I'll give you a point. [DING]

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.740
MILD DISQUIET!

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:28.220
Witty headlines!

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.340
A jump in sale of wine.

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:31.880
A jump in the sale of something.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:32.760
Lifeboats?

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:33.480
Umbrellas?

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:34.080
Wills?

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:35.500
Gas masks?

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:36.880
Point.
[DING]

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:41.560
Absolutely right. So in 1910, he essentially
caused a slight panic buy of gas masks.

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:43.120
Could be handy a few years later, eh?

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:47.260
-I refrained from making that joke.
-That's not unfair...

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:53.600
But yes, that was one of the things.
Then he wrote a series of science fiction books.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:57.160
One of which was called 'Real and Imaginary Worlds'.

00:08:57.460 --> 00:09:03.600
-I'm going to guess it was more imaginary than real.
-I can only think of one real one he knew anything about.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.180
And he was also wrong.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:09.680
Now we have talked about psychics,
 mediums and all this before

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:10.520
Several times.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:13.960
Several times, but the approach 
here was somewhat different.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.880
So are we looking for the scientific analysis of ghosts?

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:17.600
Point. [DING]

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:20.140
Yes, he was looking at it from the scientific method.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:24.280
And... for the time...  was remarkably skeptical.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:24.880
OK.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.060
There is a wonderful quote here.

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:33.500
"It is infinitely to be regretted that we cannot trust the loyalty of mediums. They almost always cheat."

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.160
How very dare he.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:39.640
That doesn't mean he didn't believe it.

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:42.040
But he was certainly very skeptical about it.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:43.360
He thought they were doing it the wrong way?

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.740
He thought it might be possible, but...

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:48.120
What he needed wasn't a medium.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:50.520
And I know it would be very hard to find in France,

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:52.520
but he needed a well done.

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:58.780
I'm not biscuiting that! I'm just... I'm not!

00:09:58.780 --> 00:09:59.920
Oh come on, that's beautiful.

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:01.080
That's good stuff.

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:03.300
It's a rare thing in France.

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:10.140
Have I mentioned before
I've actually been to a spiritualist service?

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:12.240
-Is that like a church service?
-Yeah.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:14.820
No, no, he just took his spiritualist in for a tune up(!)

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:16.320
No... no!

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:19.680
-I actually meant...
-"The readings are a bit off. They need..."

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:22.920
-I meant this as a valid question.
-Yeah, as in...

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:26.640
I went to be serviced by a spiritualist?

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:28.640
No, no, I had a day...

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.420
That's very different, Matt!

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:34.220
I can tell you now, that's not what happened!

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:39.660
No, no. I'd been out with a friend of mine.
I'd had a few. I will admit this. And I walked past.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.920
And there is a Spiritualist church, near where I lived.
 And there was a sign in the window saying...

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.280
"Display of Mediumship Tonight".

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.700
And I thought... in for a laugh!

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:48.620
Yeah, OK.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:52.540
So I snuck in. I went up, and in the first
 row of this building. It was like this... church!

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.800
They had fitted it out with pews
 and a pulpit and an altar and the lot!

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:58.560
And this bloke was stood in the pulpit, doing...

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:03.180
effectively, live spiritualist... this was the big religion of the early 20th century.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.280
This even took in Rudyard Kipling
 after his son was killed.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:10.180
There were thousands. People were really
 into it and it still hangs on in certain parts.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:11.260
Is this like the American stuff?

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:14.480
Yeah, exactly the same, yeah.
But he's doing live. It was...

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:15.720
s***!

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:20.140
I can't put it any different, it was ####!

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:22.620
I was expecting any other word there.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:28.440
I walked in. I thought, "OK, I'm... You know, there's lots of older ladies in there". And I thought, well, as the new...

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:30.220
bloke in the room...

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:32.200
if he wants to show off...

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:33.500
he's going to pick on me.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:39.180
He could... I'd had a few. I'm open to anything,
 and if he could pick something out that...

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:43.740
he doesn't know, I'll be genuinely impressed.
If nothing else, in his skill at cold reading.

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:46.980
He just stood there, and this is a
mill town in the north of England...

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:53.520
right, and goes... "Now, I'm... I'm getting the vision of someone... who worked... in a factory."

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:57.420
"Maybe on some kind of cloth... machine?"

00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:59.880
"They were called... Edith."

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:03.980
And at one point, someone would go "Oh yeah! Yeah, that's my sister's friend, when I was younger."

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:06.880
That...  far away...  a link!

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:09.580
"Now! He's saying something about money."

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.580
I mean... I could do this s***!

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:15.660
"Is there a problem with..."
There was one were he said something like

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:17.580
"Is there a problem with a child?"

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:19.360
And she's kinda, "No!"

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:23.220
"Erm? Oh, the readings are very fuzzy
 from the other side."

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:26.380
"Is there a problem with children or young people at all?"

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:27.540
"No?"

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:29.840
"It's for the future!"

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:31.820
Oh yes!

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:33.540
And that's how you do it!

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:37.240
At that point, I gave an audible "HA!" from the back.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:41.460
It was terrible. I could do it.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:44.660
Stand in front of a room. Say some old people's
 names. And if you get it wrong, just go

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:47.120
"Oh, it'll make sense one day." and carry on!

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:48.720
Is this a religion?

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:51.240
Yeah! They sang hymns and everything at the end.

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:54.540
Then had a glass of orange squash. wobbled out and got a samosa butty on the way home.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:55.280
And got what?

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:56.180
A samosa butty.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:13:00.040
How northern is that phrase?

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:05.100
It's a deep fried pastry, with spiced meat inside.

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:05.880
The Empire...

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:07.180
In a bap!

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:07.680
Yeah!

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:10.020
-Bread roll, for those...
-In a bread roll, with a bit of mint sauce.

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:12.060
The Empire made it to the north.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:14.340
That sounds nice. I want to try that now.

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:15.360
It's beautiful!

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:18.720
Don't!  No... that's... no, that's double carbs, which I...

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:19.560
Chip butty!

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:20.520
Burrito.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:21.400
Yeah, never mind.

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:21.900
Yeah!

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.820
-It's three!
-I withdraw my objection.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:26.980
The number of times I've come back, with a big
 splodge of yogurt sauce down my front after one.

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:28.100
I'm sorry, what?

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:32.300
-At least that's what I told the rest of you.
-After he'd been serviced by the Spiritualist.

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:39.660
Seriously, Flammarion was simultaneously
 quite a believer and quite a skeptic.

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:41.780
He was sure there was something.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:45.500
But, as he looked at it, he kept finding
 it can't be that, it can't be that.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:46.520
Martians!

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:48.160
Or... or Martians!

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.560
Martian canal boat dwellers.

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:52.120
Beaming their thoughts down.

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:56.580
Buy me a new pot plant or one of
 those nicely painted watering cans...

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:57.520
Gonna say that.

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.580
With a... with a plant in it.

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:01.920
That's obviously from the north of Mars.

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:04.920
Every planet has a north!
What can I tell you?

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:10.960
It's kinda sad really, because he seems to
have had the scientific method and really...

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:14.180
both wants to prove it properly. Scientifically.

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:16.440
And also really wants to believe, and is going,

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:18.720
"I'm just... there must be something there!"

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:20.640
And I'm going really high pitched. But you know?

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:23.620
Yep, that's absolutely the case.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:27.140
Had a massive influence on a number of people.

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:30.340
And has quite a few things named after him.

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:31.500
Any ideas?

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:32.760
Stars?

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:35.460
- No...
- Comets?

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:37.840
-Er... Asteroids?
-Yes! [DING]

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:38.680
A ghost?!

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:39.400
Ah...

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:40.500
Well...

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:41.220
His own ghost?!

00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:41.720
Yeah!

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:43.420
It was incredibly convenient.

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:48.200
Asteroids also named after his sister,
his niece, perhaps his first wife.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:49.280
Did he name them?

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:50.100
Er... No!

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:50.720
Oh!

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:55.340
No he's just very well respected for what he did for astronomy and for science.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:59.440
And also, not canals on Mars,
what else is named on Mars?

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:00.100
Mountains?

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:02.300
Volcanoes?

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:03.620
-The opposite...
-Valleys?

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:05.100
-There's a word...
-Craters?

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:06.720
-Point [DING] Craters. Absolutely right.
-Holes!

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:07.640
Upside down hills.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:09.700
-Holes!
-Oh yes.

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:10.780
Oh yes.

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:13.800
As we Martians... I've said too much already!

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.980
With that, congratulations Matt.
 You win this week's show.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.060
Yeah!

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:24.640
You win a highly expensive summary
of the life of an American horror actor.

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:28.440
It's Vincent Price's very pricey précis.

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:34.100
With that, we say thank you to Chris Joel.

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:35.220
Gary Brannan.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:36.720
Matt Gray.

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:38.440
I've been Tom Scott and we'll see you next time.

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:40.580
Just hit myself in the face.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:42.600
Worth it.

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:44.380
Whole day, worth it for that!

